; With --effective alone the journal is read in effective-date order, so
; the assertion that effective-primary-date-assertion.test shows holding
; under --effective --primary-date fails here: by 2021-04-01 in
; effective-date order acc1 holds 10 + 1 = 11 r, the -5 r posting being
; dated 2021-06-01.

2021-01-01 opening
    acc1               10 r
    income:opening

2021-02-01 spend
    expenses            5 r
    acc1               -5 r  ; [=2021-06-01]

2021-04-01 top up
    acc1                1 r = 6 r  ; [=2021-04-01]
    income:opening

test bal --effective -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 16:
While parsing posting:
  acc1                1 r = 6 r  ; [=2021-04-01]
                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Error: Balance assertion off by -5 r (expected to see 11 r)
end test
